// Batch 004: the SPP cost of each advancement under every rules set the
// tracker holds.
//
// A row stores the cost of one advancement, never a cumulative threshold, and
// `advancementNumber` counts skills and characteristic increases alike.
//
// CRP, CRP+ and BB2016 use fixed thresholds: reaching 6, 16, 31, 51, 76 and
// 176 SPP earns a roll on the rules set's advancement table (`table_roll`).
// Each row is the gap to the previous threshold, so the costs of a player's
// first N advancements sum to the Nth threshold:
//
//   advancement   1    2    3    4    5    6
//   threshold     6   16   31   51   76  176
//   cost          6   10   15   20   25  100
//
// BB2020, DB2021 and BB2025 price an advancement by what the coach takes, so
// they hold one row per kind for each advancement number. BB2020 and DB2021
// share these costs:
//
//   advancement                1   2   3   4   5   6
//   random_primary_skill       3   4   6   8  10  15
//   chosen_primary_skill       6   8  12  16  20  30
//   random_secondary_skill     6   8  12  16  20  30
//   chosen_secondary_skill    12  14  18  22  26  40
//   random_characteristic     18  20  24  28  32  50
//
// BB2025 has no random secondary skill option:
//
//   advancement                1   2   3   4   5   6
//   random_primary_skill       3   4   6   8  10  15
//   chosen_primary_skill       6   8  12  16  20  30
//   chosen_secondary_skill    10  12  16  20  24  34
//   random_characteristic     14  16  20  24  28  38
//
// The rules sets already exist (batch 001 declares them), so entries
// reference them under the "Name" system by bare name.
// curated-data-batch-004.spec.ts pins every cost listed here.
{
  externalSystems: [{ name: 'Name', category: 'bookkeeping' }],

